@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Player Reactions";
}

<h1 class="display-5 mb-3">Player Reactions</h1>
<p>
    Horror fans tend to come to SOMA expecting jump scares. Many of them left talking about
    the story instead. This page summarizes the common reactions from players who usually play horror games.
</p>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">What Horror Fans Praised</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>The story:</strong> Many players call it one of the strongest stories in horror games.</li>
        <li><strong>The atmosphere:</strong> The flooded, rusting station and its sound design create constant unease.</li>
        <li><strong>The dread:</strong> Players describe a lasting unease about identity and consciousness rather than quick scares.</li>
        <li><strong>The ending:</strong> The "coin toss" ending is often described as haunting and hard to forget.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">What Divided Players</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Monster encounters:</strong> Some players found the stealth sections frustrating or repetitive, especially without any way to fight back.</li>
        <li><strong>Pacing:</strong> Some wanted more fear, while others enjoyed the slow, story-driven approach.</li>
        <li><strong>Different expectations:</strong> Fans of Amnesia-style survival horror sometimes found SOMA more of a thinking game than a frightening one.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">Common Feelings After Playing</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Sadness and unease more than fear</li>
        <li>Long discussions about the "copy vs. transfer" question</li>
        <li>A wish to replay it, or to avoid replaying it</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="mb-4">
    <h2 class="h4">Safe Mode</h2>
    <p>
        The later "Safe Mode" lets players experience the story without being hunted. Some horror fans see it as
        a good way to focus on the narrative, while others prefer the original tension.
    </p>
</section>

<p class="text-muted small">
    This is a general summary of common reactions, not direct quotes. Add your own quotes from reviews or forums to personalize it.
</p>
